1
00:00:01,267 --> 00:00:04,200
♪ In the not too distant
Future ♪

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:06,967
♪ Somewhere in time and space ♪

3
00:00:06,967 --> 00:00:10,200
♪ Mike Nelson
And his robot pals ♪

4
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:13,533
♪ Are caught in a nasty place ♪

5
00:00:13,533 --> 00:00:16,433
♪ They try to survive
The wrath of Pearl ♪

6
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:19,467
♪ Just an evil gal
Who wants to rule the world ♪

7
00:00:19,467 --> 00:00:22,433
♪ From her castle below
She sets her sights above ♪

8
00:00:22,433 --> 00:00:24,100
♪ Just to torture
All the captives ♪

9
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:26,067
♪ On the Satellite of Love ♪

10
00:00:26,067 --> 00:00:29,000
Get me down!

11
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,767
♪ I’ll send him
Cheesy movies ♪

12
00:00:31,767 --> 00:00:35,100
♪ The worst I can find
La-la-la ♪

13
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:38,233
♪ He’ll have to sit
And watch them all ♪

14
00:00:38,233 --> 00:00:41,400
♪ And I’ll monitor his mind
La-la-la ♪

15
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:44,400
♪ Now keep in mind
Mike can’t control ♪

16
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:47,567
♪ Where the movies begin or end
la-la-la ♪

17
00:00:47,567 --> 00:00:50,433
♪ He’ll try to keep
His sanity ♪

18
00:00:50,433 --> 00:00:55,833
♪ With the help of
his robot friends ♪

19
00:00:55,833 --> 00:00:57,433
- Robot roll call, Cambot!

20
00:00:57,433 --> 00:00:58,433
- You’re on!

21
00:00:58,433 --> 00:00:59,800
- Gypsy!
- Oh, my stars!

22
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:01,733
- Tom Servo!
- Check me out!

23
00:01:01,733 --> 00:01:03,400
- Croooow!
- I’m different!

24
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:06,367
♪ If you’re wondering
How he eats and breathes ♪

25
00:01:06,367 --> 00:01:09,133
♪ And other science facts
La-la-la ♪

26
00:01:09,133 --> 00:01:10,733
♪ Just repeat to yourself ♪

27
00:01:10,733 --> 00:01:15,667
♪ "It’s just a show
I should really just relax" ♪

28
00:01:15,667 --> 00:01:20,533
♪ For Mystery Science
Theater 3000 ♪

29
00:01:36,233 --> 00:01:38,833
- Hi. Crow T. Robot here
on the satellite of love,

30
00:01:38,833 --> 00:01:41,200
enjoying the great taste
and satisfaction

31
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:43,367
only smokeless tobacco
can bring.

32
00:01:44,433 --> 00:01:45,433
Damn!

33
00:01:45,433 --> 00:01:47,467
Just got to work
on my aim a little.

34
00:01:47,467 --> 00:01:48,900
Doh, damn.

35
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:50,367
- Hey Crow, what’s up?

36
00:01:50,367 --> 00:01:52,033
- Flavor, Mike.
Have a dip.

37
00:01:52,033 --> 00:01:54,433
Try the Kodiak polar
ice melt menthol.

38
00:01:55,533 --> 00:01:56,867
Damn.

39
00:01:56,867 --> 00:01:58,033
- Crow, this is disgusting.

40
00:01:58,033 --> 00:02:00,233
Look at this,
tobacco juice everywhere.

41
00:02:00,233 --> 00:02:01,633
- Well, you’re just jealous

42
00:02:01,633 --> 00:02:04,300
’cause I can enjoy full flavor
whenever I go.

43
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:07,033
Say, you need me to [indistinct]
or bring down a mule-deer?

44
00:02:07,033 --> 00:02:08,200
- Ah, no.

45
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:10,700
Hey, which pop can is mine?
Do you know?

46
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:12,400
- Mmm-mmm.
Well, hell I don’t know.

47
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:13,767
Just jingle ’em all.

48
00:02:13,767 --> 00:02:15,300
There’s a lot of satisfaction
in those cans, Mike.

49
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:16,300
Nah, you know.

50
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:17,867
I think I’ll just pass,
thanks.

51
00:02:19,333 --> 00:02:21,933
- Well, I got a big load here.
Hang on.

52
00:02:24,133 --> 00:02:25,533
Woah, heh heh.

53
00:02:25,533 --> 00:02:27,367
Right down
into your shoe, Mike.

54
00:02:27,367 --> 00:02:28,833
Heh.

55
00:02:28,833 --> 00:02:31,400
- We’ll be right back.

56
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:34,300
- Oh, relax, Mike!
You just gotta learn to cope.

57
00:02:35,833 --> 00:02:37,433
Bingo!

58
00:02:37,433 --> 00:02:40,433
[♪♪♪]

59
00:02:44,467 --> 00:02:45,700
[MOANING AND CHEWING]

60
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:48,300
- There, Mike.
I’ve clearly labeled them.

61
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:49,300
Now you don’t
have to worry about

62
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:51,500
accidentally
drinking my spittle.

63
00:02:52,767 --> 00:02:54,067
- Man, have you guys tried

64
00:02:54,067 --> 00:02:56,433
this Crow’s Tobacco
Juice Brand Pop?

65
00:02:56,433 --> 00:02:58,700
It’s not that good.

66
00:02:58,700 --> 00:03:01,200
- I’m gonna let Pearl talk
while I go vomit.

67
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,467
- Okay, alright.

68
00:03:02,467 --> 00:03:04,267
- You know, the good stuff’s
on the bottom.

69
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:05,267
- Oh really?

70
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:09,767
- Okay Pearl, here we go.

71
00:03:09,767 --> 00:03:11,300
[MOANS]
That’s it, that’s it.

72
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:13,000
You’ve got the power.

73
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,400
[CRIES OUT]
Okay, dig now.

74
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:16,867
Find it, find it.

75
00:03:18,133 --> 00:03:20,433
[BEEPING]

76
00:03:20,433 --> 00:03:21,867
[MOANS]

77
00:03:21,867 --> 00:03:23,433
- Okay, home slice.

78
00:03:23,433 --> 00:03:24,600
Time for me to inflict

79
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:27,467
some brilliantly cruel
experiment on you

80
00:03:27,467 --> 00:03:31,300
and time for you to be
a helpless irredeemable moron.

81
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:33,833
- Well, okay-- Hey!

82
00:03:33,833 --> 00:03:36,600
- This week, a variant
on Dr. Harry Harlow’s famous

83
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:40,467
maternal love deprivation
experiments on monkeys.

84
00:03:40,467 --> 00:03:42,100
Only I don’t use monkeys.

85
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:43,800
I use you poor saps.

86
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:50,567
[GIGGLES]
And I begin withholding love...

87
00:03:50,567 --> 00:03:51,800
now!

88
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:53,933
Heh?
How do you like them apples?

89
00:03:53,933 --> 00:03:55,233
- Hmm.

90
00:03:55,233 --> 00:03:58,300
No, it’s status quo up here
Pearl, sorry.

91
00:03:59,367 --> 00:04:00,567
- Uh, uh, uh, Pearl?

92
00:04:00,567 --> 00:04:02,767
I’m afraid the efficacy
of the experiment

93
00:04:02,767 --> 00:04:04,833
depends on you
first administering love

94
00:04:04,833 --> 00:04:07,467
and then later
withholding it.

95
00:04:07,467 --> 00:04:08,733
- Oh.

96
00:04:08,733 --> 00:04:11,933
So, alls I gotta do is
show them love first, huh?

97
00:04:11,933 --> 00:04:14,567
Uh, okay,
love, love, love.

98
00:04:14,567 --> 00:04:16,533
Is that where you find
the least common denominator

99
00:04:16,533 --> 00:04:18,133
and then add the numerators?

100
00:04:18,133 --> 00:04:21,200
- Uh, no. That would be adding
fractions, I’m afraid.

101
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:23,633
- Well, is it where
you melt the butter

102
00:04:23,633 --> 00:04:25,633
and stir in the flour
and the salt,

103
00:04:25,633 --> 00:04:27,567
adding eggs one at a time
in the sauce pan until...

104
00:04:27,567 --> 00:04:31,400
- No, no, that’s your recipe for
puff pastry.

105
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:33,100
- Oh! I know what love is.

106
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:34,067
I saved some stuff.

107
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:36,233
- Coming up.

108
00:04:38,933 --> 00:04:40,233
[SIGHS]

109
00:04:40,233 --> 00:04:47,367
- This to me represents love.
Send it up, cream face.

110
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:50,633
- Love.

111
00:04:52,367 --> 00:04:53,667
- Huh?

112
00:04:53,667 --> 00:04:55,000
- Oh, huh.

113
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,067
So, this is Pearls love, huh?
- Oh, what do you know?

114
00:04:57,067 --> 00:04:58,900
- Staple remover.

115
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:01,133
- Pawn shop receipt
for a 10-gauge shot gun.

116
00:05:01,133 --> 00:05:02,433
- Wow.

117
00:05:02,433 --> 00:05:05,000
- A bottle of Fleishman’s
lemon flavored gin.

118
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,667
- Yummy.

119
00:05:06,667 --> 00:05:08,533
- Twelve hot pads.

120
00:05:08,533 --> 00:05:10,767
- And an alternator.

121
00:05:10,767 --> 00:05:12,667
Wow! Pearl really does love us.

122
00:05:12,667 --> 00:05:14,667
[GIGGLES]

123
00:05:14,667 --> 00:05:15,733
[LAUGHS]
No love!

124
00:05:15,733 --> 00:05:16,967
Love is gone.

125
00:05:16,967 --> 00:05:18,033
- Wow.

126
00:05:18,033 --> 00:05:20,067
Heh-heh, so lost--
feeling panicky--

127
00:05:20,067 --> 00:05:21,233
no sense of self--

128
00:05:21,233 --> 00:05:22,533
developing stress disorder

129
00:05:22,533 --> 00:05:23,533
and an inability
to work with others...

130
00:05:23,533 --> 00:05:24,533
[GROANING IN PANIC]

131
00:05:24,533 --> 00:05:26,400
- Pearl!
Please stop torturing Crow.

132
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:27,667
Give us your love back,
please!

133
00:05:27,667 --> 00:05:29,900
- Wheeeee-ere is love?

134
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:35,700
- Oh, alright.
Here’s all my love back.

135
00:05:35,700 --> 00:05:37,433
Just take it.
I don’t even care.

136
00:05:39,767 --> 00:05:40,900
- And while you’re at it,

137
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:43,233
take a hug from the warm
and nurturing film,

138
00:05:43,233 --> 00:05:46,567
The Blood Waters of Dr. Z.

139
00:05:46,567 --> 00:05:48,167
- Love, love...

140
00:05:48,167 --> 00:05:49,800
- Oh, here you go, yeah.
- Whoa, love!

141
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:50,800
- Here you go, kid.

142
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:52,667
- Sweet hot pad love.

143
00:05:52,667 --> 00:05:53,800
- There you go.

144
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:55,267
- She does love me.

145
00:05:55,267 --> 00:05:56,567
- Movie sign!
- Here we go!

146
00:05:56,567 --> 00:05:57,567
- Goodbye, love.

147
00:06:11,767 --> 00:06:13,100
MIKE:
Oh.

148
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:15,633
See, this is why I hate cats.
Look at this.

149
00:06:17,433 --> 00:06:18,700
TOM:
Oh. Flood waters, huh?

150
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:20,600
Guess Dr. Z had a little
kidney problem.

151
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:23,767
[MIKE AND CROW GIGGLING]

152
00:06:23,767 --> 00:06:25,533
[MIKE SIGHS]

153
00:06:26,633 --> 00:06:27,900
CROW:
Uh, theme music?

154
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:30,700
Anything you want to
throw in at this point?

155
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:31,933
Eh?

156
00:06:31,933 --> 00:06:32,933
TOM:
Guess not.

157
00:06:32,933 --> 00:06:34,433
CROW:
Eh?

158
00:06:34,433 --> 00:06:35,433
MIKE:
Thank you.

159
00:06:35,433 --> 00:06:36,500
That was brilliant.

160
00:06:43,333 --> 00:06:44,967
TOM:
Oh, I gotta go on a diet,

161
00:06:44,967 --> 00:06:46,367
I can’t put it off
any longer.

162
00:06:46,367 --> 00:06:47,700
[GROANS]

163
00:06:47,700 --> 00:06:51,900
Dr. Z (Voice Over):
Sargassum, the weed of deceit.

164
00:06:51,900 --> 00:06:53,100
TOM:
That’s what I smoke.

165
00:06:55,067 --> 00:06:57,000
Dr. Z (VO):
Sargassum fish...

166
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,267
MIKE:
Sarcasm fish?

167
00:06:58,267 --> 00:07:01,433
Dr. Z (VO):
...mighty hunter of the deep.

168
00:07:01,433 --> 00:07:04,467
MIKE:
Oh, I’m such a great fish.

169
00:07:04,467 --> 00:07:08,667
Dr. Z (VO):
What an inspiration,
you have been in my plot.

170
00:07:08,667 --> 00:07:09,800
TOM:
Thank you.

171
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:10,933
If I get to sit here
and suck water

172
00:07:10,933 --> 00:07:12,933
without you interrupting me.

173
00:07:12,933 --> 00:07:19,800
Dr. Z (VO)
Your life of hiding, waiting,
stalking your prey...

174
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:21,167
CROW:
Ew, Michael Jackson skin.

175
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:25,100
MIKE:
Please enjoy a fish anus.

176
00:07:28,267 --> 00:07:29,267
TOM:
Glaucoma and you.

177
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:33,633
Dr. Z (VO)
At just the right moment...

178
00:07:35,133 --> 00:07:36,900
attack!

179
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:38,200
CROW:
Uh, I was gonna do that anyway.

180
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:39,433
I don’t need coaching.

181
00:07:41,467 --> 00:07:44,533
MIKE:
Now... digest!

182
00:07:44,533 --> 00:07:46,033
Dr. Z (VO)
I love you.

183
00:07:46,033 --> 00:07:50,367
TOM: [LAUGHS]
And I love you,
but not in that way.

184
00:07:50,367 --> 00:07:53,833
Dr. Z (VO)

185
00:07:53,833 --> 00:07:55,733
CROW:
Uh, I hate it when a fish
goes down the wrong pipe.

186
00:07:55,733 --> 00:07:57,000
Blah.

187
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:00,800
MIKE:
Well, that’s the last
of my kids.

188
00:08:04,733 --> 00:08:06,900
Dr. Z (VO)
And my friend, the shark.

189
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:07,900
TOM:
Hi.

190
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:10,233
Dr. Z (VO)
Cunning, swift.

191
00:08:10,233 --> 00:08:14,267
Wretched humans,
they’re afraid of you.

192
00:08:14,267 --> 00:08:16,700
I admire you.

193
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:21,633
Soon, I’ll swim with you.
They’ll be afraid.

194
00:08:21,633 --> 00:08:23,300
[LAUGHS]

195
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:25,133
TOM:
Well, that’s one
I tell for myself.

196
00:08:25,133 --> 00:08:27,633
Dr. Z (VO)
Oh, mighty scorpion.

197
00:08:27,633 --> 00:08:30,433
Dangerous beast of the ocean.

198
00:08:30,433 --> 00:08:34,133
With your powerful daggers
and your camouflage,

199
00:08:34,133 --> 00:08:37,200
you have little to fear
from other fish.

200
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:39,400
CROW:
Yeah, well you’re kinda
blowing my cover right now.

201
00:08:43,733 --> 00:08:44,800
[LAUGHING]

202
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:45,967
MIKE:
What?

203
00:08:45,967 --> 00:08:48,433
Dr. Z (VO)
They think I’m insane.

204
00:08:48,433 --> 00:08:51,800
They’re the ones
who are insane!

205
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:53,933
Oh, my friends of the deep.

206
00:08:53,933 --> 00:08:55,933
TOM:
Just tap some fish flakes in
and then leave.

207
00:08:55,933 --> 00:09:00,867
Dr. Z (VO)
This day, this very day,
I’ll become one of you.

208
00:09:00,867 --> 00:09:03,200
CROW:
Yeah, we’re really excited
about it down here.

209
00:09:06,733 --> 00:09:09,233
MIKE: [IMITATING WEEPING]
Oh, no one will hug me.

210
00:09:11,667 --> 00:09:13,067
Dr. Z (VO)
My family.

211
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:17,567
TOM:
And you, balding
comb over fish.

212
00:09:17,567 --> 00:09:21,500
Dr. Z (VO)
And together,
we’ll conquer the universe.

213
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:22,967
CROW:
Or my one-room
basement apartment

214
00:09:22,967 --> 00:09:24,267
I share with mother.

215
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:31,833
MIKE:
But first, a folk song
by Phil Ochs.

216
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:41,100
CROW:
It’s got playful
teen beach movie font.

217
00:09:47,233 --> 00:09:52,367
TOM:
♪ Oh Dr. Z won’t you love me ♪

218
00:09:52,367 --> 00:09:56,367
♪ In World War II boy ♪

219
00:09:56,367 --> 00:09:58,100
MIKE:
Sounds like the indigo boys.

220
00:10:03,167 --> 00:10:05,700
CROW:
Well, I guess I better
get back to world domination.

221
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:09,633
♪ For all the missing
With your luck ♪

222
00:10:09,633 --> 00:10:12,400
TOM:
He doesn’t inspire
this kind of music.

223
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:17,833
♪ Keeps you up at night ♪

224
00:10:17,833 --> 00:10:20,133
MIKE:
Where the hell is my house?

225
00:10:20,133 --> 00:10:25,200
♪ Their moon tangles
Both your feet ♪

226
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:27,400
CROW:
This is the leakiest damn pool.

227
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:32,767
♪ Drags you down helplessly
Toward your fate ♪

228
00:10:32,767 --> 00:10:34,500
MIKE: [IMITATING]
Well, that was fun.

229
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:40,133
♪ Tombstones are piling up
Your last mistake ♪

230
00:10:40,133 --> 00:10:42,000
MIKE:
I should rotate my bodies,
I guess.

231
00:10:43,633 --> 00:10:49,533
♪ Give us a break
Give us a break ♪

232
00:10:49,533 --> 00:10:50,500
CROW:
Give us a break!

233
00:10:53,167 --> 00:10:55,200
TOM:
Yeah, this is obviously
Switzerland.

234
00:11:00,133 --> 00:11:03,933
MIKE:
My Sustical has made me
the dynamo I am today.

235
00:11:03,933 --> 00:11:08,767
♪ Sashay sashay
Through the sarcasm ♪

236
00:11:08,767 --> 00:11:11,067
CROW:
Oh, I’m really gonna sashay
through the sarcasm.

237
00:11:11,067 --> 00:11:16,300
♪ ...skulking
Through the sarcasm ♪

238
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:22,333
♪ Planning revenge
On your friends ♪

239
00:11:22,333 --> 00:11:23,400
MIKE:
Oh, I would never do that.

240
00:11:27,667 --> 00:11:28,667
CROW:
Oh, go on with you.

241
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:35,967
TOM: [HUMMING]
Planning revenge on my friends.

242
00:11:35,967 --> 00:11:37,433
[HUMMING]

243
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:41,433
MIKE:
Well, he’s got
an egg shaped head.

244
00:11:45,833 --> 00:11:47,733
CROW:
That song put the boogie
in my feet.

245
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:54,967
MIKE:
He’s got
the Gwyneth Paltrow haircut.

246
00:11:57,133 --> 00:11:58,800
TOM:
Should I perform
horrible experiments

